/* ============================================================
 * APS REFERENCE LETTER — MASTER TEMPLATE (Google Doc)
 *
 * The letter's wording, letterhead logo, and Principal's signature all live
 * in ONE master Google Doc — REFERENCE_LETTER_TEMPLATE_DOC_ID below — not in
 * this file. An Administrator can open that Doc any time and edit the
 * wording/design directly; the very next generated letter picks up the
 * change automatically, with no code deployment required.
 *
 * generateReferenceLetterPdf_() makes a temporary copy of that Doc, fills in
 * the placeholders below via Body.replaceText(), exports the copy to PDF,
 * then trashes the copy. Both the Teacher self-request flow
 * (submitReferenceLetterRequest()) and the Admin-initiated flow
 * (submitAdminInitiatedReferenceLetter()) share this SAME master template —
 * there is only one letter design for all Teaching Volunteers. letterType
 * (REFERENCE_LETTER_TYPE.STANDARD / .VOLUNTEER) is still recorded per
 * request for audit/reporting, it just no longer selects a different
 * template.
 *
 * Placeholders the master Doc may contain (exact spelling, case-sensitive):
 *   {{TEACHER_NAME}}   {{APSID}}   {{APS_JOIN_DATE}}   {{ISSUE_DATE}}
 * Do NOT add {{REQUEST_REASON}} or {{REQUEST_DATE}} to the Doc — the
 * approved letter design intentionally omits the requester's stated reason;
 * that reason is still captured and kept in the audit Sheet (see
 * requestReason below), it is simply never printed on the letter itself.
 * ============================================================ */
// Sept 2026, fifty-fourth round: moved to Script Properties — set
