/* ==========================================================================
 *  r117 — ONE WEEKLY-JOBS SCHEDULER (Apps Script allows only 20 triggers per user per project)
 *
 *  One hourly trigger `apsWeeklyJobs` runs every weekly job at its usual time instead of one trigger per job:
 *    Sun ~2 AM   System backup & audit archive          (was apsWeeklyMaintenance)
 *    Mon ~7 AM   Students in more than one classroom    (was apsWeeklyMultipleClassroomReport, ~7:30)
 *    Tue ~8 AM   Grading Help Team report               (was apsMissingGradingWeekly, ~8:30)
 *    Wed ~9 AM   Continuous student absence             (was apsStudentAbsenceWeekly, ~9:30)
 *    Wed ~7 PM   Class consolidation analysis           (was apsClassConsolidationAnalysis)
 *    Wed ~7 PM   Weekly Teacher Appreciation            (was apsTeacherAppreciationWeekly)
 *    Wed ~7:30+  Class consolidation email              (was apsClassConsolidationEmail; ≥ 25 min after the analysis)
 *  A job runs in the first hourly check at or after its hour and at most once per week (state in Script Property
 *  APS_WEEKLY_JOBS_STATE — one small JSON, one entry per job). A missed run is caught up for 24 hours; a failed run
 *  is retried on the next checks (max 3 attempts). Several due jobs run one after another while the run is young
 *  (a new job starts only within the first minute; each job keeps its own time budget); the rest follow next hour.
 *  The jobs keep their school-leave guards and their own locks / idempotency. Setting up (apsEnsureWeeklyJobsTrigger_,
 *  on Admin visits and from the old "create…Trigger" editor tools) deletes the absorbed per-job triggers FIRST, then
 *  makes sure exactly one apsWeeklyJobs trigger exists. A first install marks this week's already-passed slots as done
 *  (no surprise catch-up). An old per-job trigger that still fires after the move does nothing (MOVED_TO_WEEKLY_JOBS).
 *  Log sheet APS_WEEKLY_JOBS_LOG (one row per job run; trimmed to the newest 1000 rows).
 * ========================================================================== */
